Four hard boundaries plus the flow: (1) the token can only ever reach a machine-registered origin; (2) the Gitea path never invokes `gh` and never degrades to GitHub; (3) an unreadable CI status is *unknown*, never a pass; (4) undeclared-platform repos behave exactly as before. I tested each of these with harnesses I wrote myself, not only the builder's.

